NAME
    continue - skip to the next iteration of the nearest enclosing loop

SYNOPSIS
    continue

DESCRIPTION
    A hardcoded, zero-argument parser keyword, same as 'break'. Skips the
    rest of the current loop body and re-evaluates the loop's own condition
    (or advances to the next word, for 'for'). Outside any loop it's a
    silent no-op, matching bash.
